comments.body:
@participant7 Thanks for providing a workaround solution while we're working on a fix.

@participant8 Thanks for sharing your investigation. 

I've come to the conclusion that the native input path does not provide enough support for advanced use cases and that it's better to move Windows Terminal to the VT input path. While this was the original suggestion here, there was a slight caveat in that the input path gate was checked in 2 different locations. Failing to update both checks to include WT_SESSION in addition to TERM would produce unreliable results (because of setup code that would override some options).

I've opened a PR with the fix. As noted in the PR, the new path makes multi-line pasting available for applications/shells that support it, namely wsl/bash, vim, Claude CLI and other TUIs that have proper bracketed paste support. Notably, cmd, pwsh and nushell do not support bracketed paste (with or without zellij).
